            "description": "Watch Hammarby vs Anderlecht highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 23, 2026. High stakes defined the atmosphere in Stockholm for this UEFA Europa League clash on 2026-07-23 as Hammarby hosted Anderlecht . Both sides entered the pitch with everything to play for in a match characterized by tactical discipline and sudden shifts in momentum. Early Pressure and Defensive Grit The visitors wasted no time asserting their dominance. In the 6th minute, Danylo Sikan found the back of the net to give Anderlecht an early lead, a goal that immediately put Hammarby on the back foot. The first half subsequently devolved into a gritty battle in the middle of the park, with the referee busy managing a series of fouls. Yellow cards were issued to Nathan Saliba , Ludwig Augustinsson , and Frederik Winther before the break, as the intensity of the competition led to several heated exchanges and limited clear-cut chances for the home side. Red Card and Tactical Reshuffle The second half began with similar intensity, as Victor Eriksson went into the book almost immediately after the restart. The game reached its major turning point in the 78th minute when Nathan Saliba received his second yellow card and was sent off, leaving Anderlecht to defend their lead with ten men. Sensing an opportunity, the hosts made several changes, including the introduction of Frank Junior Adjei for Victor Lind in the 86th minute. Meanwhile, the visitors brought on Zoumana Keita and Noah Kalonji in an attempt to shore up their defense and see out the result. Dramatic Equalizer at the Death With the clock ticking toward full time, the home side’s persistence finally paid off. In the 89th minute, Paulos Abraham provided a decisive assist for Frank Junior Adjei , who clinicaly finished to level the score. The late strike electrified the stadium and rewarded Hammarby for their relentless pressure following the red card. 